== Overview ==
As the name suggests, Endless Mode is a mode with an infinite number of waves, where you are tasked with getting as far as you can without losing to the toilets. There will be rewards when you beat a wave. It is confirmed by Telanthric that completing at least 50% of one wave can get the reward of the wave.  

{{Notice|This mode is much harder than [[Nightmare Mode|Nightmare]] mode, replacing Nightmare as the hardest mode}}
== Strategy ==

Use units with high DPS, units with slowing, and units with time stop for an ideal loadout. 

A few recommended units are Green Laser Cameraman, [[Hyper Upgraded Titan Speakerman|Hyper UTS]], Large Clockman, [[Astro Upgraded Titan Cameraman|Astro UTC]], and Santa TV Man. These units are very powerful and will ensure you get a high wave in Endless, since they have good support and damage.

Healer units are also very useful for the large amounts of stuns in Endless. They ensure your units are not stunned and can deal the most amounts of damage, which is needed for Endless.

Booster units are unlike any other unit. Instead of giving money, DPS, or slowing, they give boosts to your units. [[Announcer Cameraman]], or, if you can afford it, [[DJ TV Man]] or [[Titan Warlord Clockman]], are very helpful in Endless since they boost your unit's damage by a large amount.

This mode is not recommended for grinding coins, but instead, this mode is great for grinding Endless XP and Clan Coins.

